    "body": "Prepare the directly affected native Testkit callers for the pending 0.51 hard cut: fixture input records use fields, and typed query/update operations carry an explicit principal under one method name per operation. Preserve existing principal choices, reply-decoding budgets and operation ordering.\n\nThis is a draft caller patch. Integrate with published Testkit 0.51 and update the normal dependency selection before merging. This contribution deliberately changes no manifest requirement, selected normal lockfile, own package version or stored product format.\n\nValidation: directly affected caller compilation on Rust 1.99 (the benchmark package declares that floor), strict affected-target Clippy, Rustfmt and patch checks pass against the prepared Testkit source through an isolated temporary source override. The override and qualified lock graph are excluded from the PR. These compile/lint checks do not establish installed application or native macOS acceptance; no broad local suite was run. Testkit's producer separately passes focused codec/retry/benchmark tests and live call/install/snapshot/ownership qualification with prepared PocketIC 16.1.\n\nThe normal sibling checkout and its pending work remain untouched.\n",
